{
  "id": "vikings",
  "name": "Vikings",
  "abbr": "vik",
  "slug": "vikings",
  "classes": "Longhouses, Infantry, Sagas",
  "description": "The Vikings are raiders from the north that overwhelmed their enemies with powerful melee infantry that could live off enemy lands. Their flexible Longhouses allow them to build up their population and economy with ease. Sagas and the Norse religion inspire their warriors to fight without fear for the honor of the gods.",
  "overview": [
    {
      "title": "Civilization Bonuses",
      "list": [
        "Sagas can grant bonuses by accomplishing various quests.",
        "Villagers are automatically recruited from Town Centers up to the Villager Capacity which can be increased by building Longhouses.",
        "Longhouses can be upgraded with various attachments and recruit Bondi.",
        "The Völur unit can increase the production speed of Longhouses or set up Sacred Groves on Relics.",
        "Military infantry can heal by consuming Food from Food deposits.",
        "The Vikings lack Stone walls, but palisades can be upgraded to Danevirke walls that take less fire damage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sagas",
      "description": "Sagas are quests that can be completed at any time which will unlock permanent bonuses."
    },
    {
      "title": "Northern Migration",
      "description": "Town Centers automatically recruit Villagers at no cost up to the Villager Capacity. The Villager Capacity is increased by +10 for each Longhouse constructed."
    },
    {
      "title": "Longhouse",
      "description": "Longhouses can be upgraded with one of four different attachments. The Farmstead adds two vegetable fields, which have a higher gather rate than normal Farms. The Bee Skeps will passively generate gold. Looms will automatically improve the armor of military units. The Smithy will automatically improve the damage of military units."
    },
    {
      "title": "Völur",
      "description": "Völur are support units that can travel between Longhouses, boosting the production of Bee Skeps and Farmsteads for a duration. The Völur can also be sacrificed to establish a Sacred Grove on Relics, which passively recruits Berserkers and has an aura that increases the armor of nearby units."
    },
    {
      "title": "Bondi",
      "description": "Bondi are unique spearmen that have increased health and armor. When Bondi are near each other, they gain a Shield Wall buff temporarily increasing their health."
    },
    {
      "title": "Berserker",
      "description": "The Berserker is a unique light armor unit that has high damage, fast movement speed, and is armed with two axes. Berserkergang is triggered at low health, which regenerates health and increases damage."
    },
    {
      "title": "Living Off The Land",
      "description": "Military infantry can heal themselves by gathering Food from deposits such as Berry Bushes, Deer or Boar."
    },
    {
      "title": "Longship and Drakkar",
      "description": "The Longship is a unique archer ship that also acts as a transport, each loaded unit increases the arrows fired and increases health. The Drakkar replaces the Springald Ship and can throw nets on enemy ships to slow them down."
    },
    {
      "title": "Influence",
      "description": "Construct Longhouses within the Dock's influence to reduce the cost of ships in all Docks by 4% for each Longhouse up to a maximum of 16%."
    }
  ],
